From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 18:24:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 29/30] Typer, Solver: fixes from the attack on headsubst

- An associated type that a conformance does not define is selected through
  the witness; it is never the error type, which is equal to every type.
- The solver fails, with a diagnostic, when an associated type of a callee's
  requirement cannot be determined.
- A function used as a value has its head bound to its premises, so that a
  selection through its requirement written in the scope of use decides the
  witness passed; only the callee of a call is matched against the solver's
  opened copy.
- A coercion to a type that mentions an unresolved associated type waits, also
  when the variable was unified with another one or occurs inside the type.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Mythos 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011CH6tJP7hLkrpGFxEq7K6r
